#usda 1.0
(
    defaultPrim = "InfeedScannerVisual"
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Z"
    doc = """Visual-only tunnel shroud for the conveyor infeed / outfeed port.

    References the NVIDIA DigitalTwin baggage scanner, the only warehouse asset
    that ships both a tunnel opening and lead-rubber curtains, so the belt reads
    as if it comes out of (or runs into) a machine instead of ending in mid air.

    Physics: the referenced source was audited offline with pxr and carries
    zero PhysicsCollisionAPI / PhysicsRigidBodyAPI / Physx* schemas on all 97
    prims, so this wrapper has nothing to strip and deliberately authors no
    physics attributes at all.  It is spawned through AssetBaseCfg + UsdFileCfg
    without collision_props / rigid_props, which keeps it out of PhysX, out of
    reset, and out of the ZMQ scene-sync inventory.

    Units: like the Tote_B04 wrapper next to this file, the source is authored
    in centimetre units (its own stage declares metersPerUnit = 0.01 and has no
    compensating root scale).  This layer keeps metersPerUnit = 1 to match the
    task stage and lets the task apply the 0.01 authored-unit -> metre factor
    through UsdFileCfg.scale, so the whole scale budget stays in
    ``shroud_config.SHROUD_UNIT_SCALE`` / ``SHROUD_DESIGN_SCALE``.

    Measured local geometry after that 0.01 factor (origin = machine centre,
    sitting on the floor plane):
        overall   x +/-0.42161  y +/-1.27424  z 0 .. 1.50206
        roller / belt top surface           z = 0.851355
        curtain opening                     z 0.855965 .. 1.340204, 0.6316 wide
        tunnel cabinet (floor standing)     y +/-0.350363
    """
)

def Xform "InfeedScannerVisual" (
    prepend references = @https://omniverse-content-production.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/Assets/Isaac/5.1/NVIDIA/Assets/DigitalTwin/Assets/Warehouse/Equipment/Security/BaggageScanner_A/SecurityBaggageScanner_A01_01.usd@
)
{
}
